Extropian unit mlshew@netcom.com (Mark Shewmaker) says:
> Of course, adding a second stack of your own topics-list, perhaps
> with a multiwindow editor, adds even more functionality to the
> scheme, but still keeping it mind-boggingly simple.

Besides remembering items on a list, try remembering also the *number* of 
items on your list.  Then when you're trying to recall your items you can 
count them off.  This way you will always know if you are finished with 
your list or not.  When most people forget to pick up something at the 
store, its because they picked up most items and thought they were done.  
They did not rack their brains trying to figure out what the last item was.  
Most people will be able to remember the lost item if they know for certain 
that there was one more item on the list.
